Fold re-verify (driver: fold-recheck.py, this dir; frames foldr-*.png):
Harness lessons (recorded so the next pass does not re-learn them):
1. The env MUST strip WAYLAND_DISPLAY/XDG_SESSION_TYPE: Tauri takes the real
   Wayland session otherwise and silently ignores Xvfb's DISPLAY (zero windows
   on the private display).
2. No WM on Xvfb => the window opens at Tauri's default 1100x720; the fold
   test must pin it with `xdotool windowsize <wid> W H` or it measures the
   wrong box.
3. Focused-footer-button key activation (Return/Space via XTEST) is ignored by
   WebKitGTK in this harness; use XTEST mouse on the driver's own display.

